## Cross-Verification & Audit Notes

**PAT (IGAAP) reconciliation:** Investor deck shows ₹(5.8) Cr; statutory filing (Sr.7, "Net Profit after tax," YTD Sep-24) shows Rs. (580) lakhs = ₹(5.8) Cr — **exact match**.

**NWP/NEP reconciliation:** Deck NWP of ₹2,544.9 Cr matches statutory Sr.2 ("Net Premium Written") of 2,544,498 lakhs = ₹2,544.98 Cr. Deck NEP of ₹2,231.2 Cr matches statutory Sr.3 ("Premium Earned (Net)") of 2,231,124 lakhs = ₹2,231.12 Cr.

**Net worth reconciliation:** Deck figure of ₹2,064.6 Cr matches statutory Analytical Ratios Sr.6 ("Net Worth") of 2,06,455 lakhs = ₹2,064.55 Cr.

**Important discrepancy flag — EoM ratio:** Two different bases exist for this metric, and they should not be treated as interchangeable:
- Statutory filing's own Analytical Ratios table reports "Expense of Management to Net Written Premium Ratio" = **50.95%** for YTD Sep-24.
- Investor deck reports "Expense of Management as % of GWP" = **40.0%**.

These are calculated on different denominators (EoM/NWP vs. EoM/GWP, the latter excluding the 1/n adjustment per the deck's own footnote). Per the statutory IGAAP preference rule, **50.95%** (EoM/NWP) is the figure reported in the table above.

**Commission ratio:** Not disclosed as a standalone ratio in either source. It has been independently derived from statutory YTD figures — Net Commission (₹508.29 Cr) ÷ NWP (₹2,544.98 Cr) = **19.97%**. This is a fully sourced calculation from statutory line items, not an estimate.

**Regulatory risk flag — EoM forbearance:** The statutory filing's Note 6 discloses that Niva Bupa exceeded the regulatory EoM limit for FY23 and FY24 and has an outstanding forbearance application pending with IRDAI (a show-cause notice was issued on October 18, 2024). ₹162.05 Cr of excess EoM was transferred from the Revenue Account to the P&L Account for H1FY25 — this represents a material regulatory/compliance risk that should be factored into any credit or equity analysis of the company.</ans>
